1
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:28,583
I was born over 71 years ago in Jerusalem.

2
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:32,663
I fought the two wars that
decided the fate of Israel,

3
00:00:33,113 --> 00:00:36,100
the fate of Jerusalem,
as the capital of Israel.

4
00:00:51,267 --> 00:00:57,297
Know the real face, the ugly face of war,

5
00:00:58,307 --> 00:01:01,077
the misery, the suffering.

6
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:17,790
Because we are looking to have
the peace of the brave men.

7
00:01:24,067 --> 00:01:29,017
Ladies and gentlemen, the
time for peace has come.

8
00:03:27,033 --> 00:03:29,283
When he hung up, he called
me back five minutes later.

9
00:03:29,493 --> 00:03:30,923
He said he was shot.

10
00:03:32,013 --> 00:03:33,983
And while he was talking,
he said, he died.

11
00:04:15,167 --> 00:04:20,797
To have known him, to
have worked with him,

12
00:04:20,827 --> 00:04:26,057
as a brother, as a friend, and as a man.

13
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:39,630
The sight you see before you was impossible
was unthinkable just three years ago.

14
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:42,600
Only poets dreamt of it.

15
00:04:45,067 --> 00:04:48,197
Your Prime Minister
was a martyr for peace,

16
00:04:48,987 --> 00:04:51,537
but he was a victim of hate.

17
00:04:52,827 --> 00:04:55,267
Surely we must learn from his martyrdom.

18
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:04,900
Grandpa, you were the pillar of fire before the camp,

19
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:09,400
and now we're just a camp left alone in the dark,

20
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:11,900
and we're so cold.

21
00:05:22,633 --> 00:05:30,133
The blood that ran out of your body
in the last moments of your life,

22
00:05:30,233 --> 00:05:35,733
is between the lines,
between the words.

23
00:05:38,567 --> 00:05:46,617
V 'al kol Yisrael, V 'imru
Amen, and Shalom Ha 'vair.

24
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:07,410
Amir appeared confident, making no
attempt to hide from the waiting media.

25
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:10,900
In fact, a policeman had to stop
him from talking to reporters.

26
00:06:44,733 --> 00:06:49,143
Meanwhile, the Israeli police minister has
called for a state inquiry into how the

27
00:06:49,173 --> 00:06:50,623
gunman managed to kill Mr.

28
00:06:50,653 --> 00:06:52,263
Rabin at point blank range.

29
00:07:31,867 --> 00:07:34,337
A question that's already
being asked here in Israel,

30
00:07:34,807 --> 00:07:37,977
a country that's been decades looking
for the enemies outside its borders,

31
00:07:38,347 --> 00:07:40,867
perhaps it wasn't looking close
enough for the enemies within.
